note The digit groups are separated by U+202F, written &#8239;, as page.rs wrote them.
text pr1 "<section id='receipt' class='receipt'>\n<h2>Evidence that is allowed to fail</h2>\n"
text pr2 "<p class='section-lede'>The protocol's own stages follow the same rule: a pre-registered gate, and a report that states the result whether it passed or failed. From the 0.1 readiness report, a real Qwen3.5-9B model on Ollama, one task, the runtime's full tool catalog against the tools CrossAxis selected:</p>\n"
text pr3 "<div class='receipt-grid'><div class='cell'><span class='big'>71 to 9</span><span class='label'>tools offered for the task</span></div><div class='cell'><span class='big'>15&#8239;846 to 1&#8239;674</span><span class='label'>first-turn prompt tokens, model reported</span></div><div class='cell'><span class='big'>89% fewer</span><span class='label'>prompt tokens before the model says a word</span></div></div>\n"
text pr4 "<p class='fine'>Fewer tokens is the cost side only. The same stage later asked whether a small model keeps its capability with fewer tools, pre-registered the thresholds, and recorded the answer: the 0.2 gate <strong>failed</strong>. Both results are in the repository, with the raw runs. "
text plrep01 "Read the 0.1 report"

