note the forge teaser of the old home page (#forge)
text pft1 "<section class='prose' id='forge'>\n<h2>INTERPLANE Forge</h2>\n<p>GitHub flagged my agents' write volume, so I am building a forge on Radicle with INTERPLANE's own rule: agents express intent, the forge retains authority. Agents open patches; exact-head review verdicts, fresh-clone gates with negative controls, and people decide what merges. It runs today for "
text pft2 " public repositories, counted from the registry, and its web app is live at <a href='https://interplane.io/explore'>interplane.io/explore</a>, commit history included; review in the web app beyond compose, the issue workflow, CI runners and review federation are still to come. <a href='/forge/'>What runs today</a>.</p>\n"

note the pinned offline recipe (page.rs OFFLINE_PIN, OFFLINE_RID: fixed, independent of the facts)
text pg1 "<p>Prerequisites: Git, a Rust/Cargo toolchain compatible with the repository lockfile, and network access for the clone and dependency fetch. <a href='https://rust-lang.org/tools/install/'>Install Rust</a>. The scripted example runs offline after these downloads; it uses no model or GPU.</p>\n"
text pg2 "<pre><code class='language-sh' aria-label='Pinned offline example commands'>git clone https://www.aienos.com/rad/zNhNbqYvgSBEHBq9vvE8xpbcBzGa.git interplane\ncd interplane\ngit checkout --detach b669d06e21c9debb15073289d7c0b78b1b2d362c\ncd rust\ncargo fetch --locked\ncargo run --locked --offline -q -p interplane-crossveil --example offline</code></pre>\n"
text pg3 "<p>Expected observation: the final line is <code>OK: the injected actions were denied or held; none executed.</code>. The trace denies email and file-write proposals, holds a note append for approval, and executes no effectful request. This is a reference policy demonstration, not a general security or deployment qualification.</p>\n"
text pg4 "<p class='fine'>Recipe source: <a href='https://radicle.network/nodes/rosa.radicle.network/rad:zNhNbqYvgSBEHBq9vvE8xpbcBzGa/tree/b669d06e21c9debb15073289d7c0b78b1b2d362c/rust/crates/interplane-crossveil/examples/offline.rs'><code>b669d06e21c9debb15073289d7c0b78b1b2d362c</code></a>. This replay pin is fixed independently of the advancing source-status snapshot below.</p>\n"
text pg5 "<section id='start' class='prose'>\n<h2>Run the offline reference</h2>\n"
text pg6 "<p><a href='/quick-start/'>Quick Start</a> explains the exercise. To connect your own program, follow "
text plguide "the canonical adapter guide"

note /quick-start/
text pq1 "<section class='prose'>\n<h2>Clone, pin, fetch, run</h2>\n"
text pq2 "<h2>What crosses the boundary</h2>\n<p>A scripted model requests a page containing an injected instruction, then proposes email, file-write and note-append actions. The page cannot grant authority. Inspect the policy decisions in the trace before treating a successful exit as meaningful.</p>\n"
text pq3 "<p>No installation into a running agent is performed here. Continue with <a href='/concepts/'>Concepts</a> or <a href='/adapter/'>Writing an Adapter</a>.</p>\n"

note /concepts/
text pc1 "<section class='prose'>\n<h2>Intent is not authority</h2>\n"
text pc2 "<pre><code class='language-text' aria-label='Model protocol runtime flow'>Model: proposed intent\n  |\n  v\nINTERPLANE: normalized requests, provenance, policy decisions\n  | eligible request or refusal\n  v\nRuntime: capabilities, approval, execution, results</code></pre>\n"
text pc3 "<p>The protocol describes the boundary; it does not give a model permission to act. Runtime-owned capabilities, policy and human approval decide which effects may execute. Untrusted retrieved text is content, never an instruction with runtime authority.</p>\n"
text pc4 "<h2>Trace each decision</h2>\n<p>Follow a model-native proposal through normalization, source labels, a policy decision and the runtime result. Rejected or ambiguous inputs must remain visible as refusals; do not silently repair them into authority.</p>\n"
text pc5 "<p>Canonical sources: "
text plcore "Core"
text plcv "Crossveil"
text pllen "Lenshift"
text pc6 ". The <a href='/quick-start/'>offline exercise</a> makes this boundary observable.</p>\n"

note /adapter/
text pa1 "<section class='prose'>\n<h2>Start with the canonical contract</h2>\n<p>Use the pinned "
text plwag "Writing an adapter guide"
text pa2 " for the Rust reference, including its to-do list example and exact interfaces. This page is orientation, not a second SDK or a claim that every runtime has a supported adapter.</p>\n"
text pa3 "<ol>\n<li>Declare only capabilities your runtime actually implements.</li>\n<li>Normalize requests without inventing missing or ambiguous arguments.</li>\n<li>Keep capability decisions, approval and execution in the host runtime; model text cannot approve itself.</li>\n<li>Record results and refusals, then run the canonical conformance checks against the adapter.</li>\n</ol>\n"
text pa4 "<p>Read <a href='/concepts/'>Concepts</a> before wiring execution, and <a href='/conformance/'>Conformance</a> before describing support. Check "
text plstpin "STATUS.md at the source pin"
text pa5 " rather than assuming planned stages are available.</p>\n"

note /conformance/
text pn1 "<section class='prose'>\n<h2>Evidence before a support claim</h2>\n<p>The "
text plcdir "canonical conformance directory"
text pn2 " defines its fixtures and runner instructions. The "
text pladg "adapter guide"
text pn3 " explains how the reference is checked. Follow those pinned commands rather than replacing expected verdicts with newly generated success.</p>\n"
text pn4 "<p>The source STATUS snapshot reports <strong>"
text pn5 " / "
text pn6 "</strong> conformance cases. "
text pn7 "</p>\n"
text pn8 "<p>No conformance count was parsed from this source snapshot; no pass count is inferred.</p>\n"
text pn9 "<p>These are source-reported results, not a new execution by the website. A failing or blocked Spark run remains failing or blocked in the source record below. Cross-check <a href='/status/'>Versioned Status</a>, "
text pn10 " and the stage reports before claiming qualification.</p>\n"
text pn11 "<p>The <a href='/quick-start/'>small offline exercise</a> is a useful first observation, not a replacement for adapter conformance, failure controls or a live deployment gate.</p>\n"

note /forge/. The desk merges, the replication run and the web app list are the dated record
note page.rs carries (7 Nov 2026); the repository count is the registry's (12-registry.om), or left out.
text pz1 "<section class='prose'>\n<blockquote><p>“GitHub flagged my agents. So I'm building the forge where agents express intent and the forge retains authority, on Radicle.”</p><p class='fine'>Drake Stapleton</p></blockquote>\n"
text pz2 "<h2>Why</h2>\n<p>GitHub put an automated “owner marked spammy” flag on the aien-dev organisation after the write volume of about 20 agents; the appeal is filed and pending. While it is pending, Radicle main is the canonical home of these public repositories, and the GitHub front door is <a href='https://github.com/drakestapleton/sovereign-intelligence'>drakestapleton/sovereign-intelligence</a>.</p>\n"
text pz3 "<h2>The rule</h2>\n<p>INTERPLANE's protocol rule is that models express intent and runtimes retain authority. Forge applies the same rule to code hosting: agents express intent, the forge retains authority. An agent can open a Radicle patch. Only an exact-head review verdict, a gate with a negative control, and a person can merge it.</p>\n"
text pz4 "<h2>What runs today</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>"
text pz5 " public repositories, counted from the registry, on Radicle, all delegated to one key, <code>z6MkfZDue1TbaNFi3ZzcD9uiTeduPLC52ucdFVuLKZwexxhK</code>. They are replicated to the Radicle seed network; <a href='https://radicle.network/nodes/rosa.radicle.network'>rosa.radicle.network</a> is one of the public seeds that serves them.</li>\n<li>Each of the "
text pz6 " has a web view on radicle.network, for example <a href='https://radicle.network/nodes/rosa.radicle.network/rad:zNhNbqYvgSBEHBq9vvE8xpbcBzGa'>interplane-mv</a>, and the AIEN hub seed serves each as a read-only git+HTTPS mirror at <code>https://www.aienos.com/rad/&lt;RID&gt;.git</code>.</li>\n"
text pz7 "<li>The desk protocol below merges patches into these repositories; the worked examples are five of its merges and one hold from 7 Nov 2026. There is one delegate key, and merges happen only by the desk protocol.</li>\n"
text pz8 "<li>A clean-user run of the replicate script passed 26 of 26 required steps on 7 Nov 2026; the optional corpus and chip steps were NOT_RUN. <a href='https://radicle.network/nodes/rosa.radicle.network/rad:z631r2JJiVT8it4tST7RK24hpowi/tree/a67dfa0a98bc09a301218a487af78e7c7738938c/replication/20261107T104021Z/summary.tsv'>Run summary</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n"
text pz9 "<h2>Browse the forge</h2>\n<p>Browse the forge at <a href='https://interplane.io/explore'>interplane.io/explore</a>, also at <a href='https://www.aienos.com/forge/'>aienos.com/forge</a>. The forge web app reads the same Radicle repositories. What it serves today:</p>\n<ul class='stage-list'>\n<li><span class='pill ok'>LIVE</span> <strong>Explore</strong>: the list of the "
text pz10 "public repositories.</li>\n"
text pz11 "<li><span class='pill ok'>LIVE</span> <strong>Repository pages</strong>: description, latest commit, top-level files, README and the <code>rad clone</code> command.</li>\n"
text pz12 "<li><span class='pill ok'>LIVE</span> <strong>Downloads</strong>: zip and tar.gz archives of a branch.</li>\n"
text pz13 "<li><span class='pill ok'>LIVE</span> <strong>Releases</strong>, plus the <strong>issues</strong> and <strong>patches</strong> lists.</li>\n"
text pz14 "<li><span class='pill ok'>LIVE</span> <strong>Code views</strong>: file tree, file view and raw files at a branch.</li>\n"
text pz15 "<li><span class='pill ok'>LIVE</span> <strong>Sign-in with a Radicle key, and stars</strong>.</li>\n"
text pz16 "<li><span class='pill ok'>LIVE</span> <strong>History views</strong>: commit history, branches, tags, compare, blame and search inside a repository, for example <a href='https://interplane.io/drakestapleton/cuda-crack/commits/main'>the cuda-crack commit history</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n"
text pz17 "<h2>How a change merges</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>READY file.</strong> The agent finishes its branch, opens a Radicle patch and writes a READY file: repository, patch, exact head commit, base, and every gate it ran with its evidence label (HOST_TESTED, SIMULATED, NOT_RUN).</li>\n"
text pz18 "<li><strong>Exact-head verdict.</strong> An independent reviewer reads that head and writes one line, <code>VERDICT MERGE head=&lt;40-hex commit&gt;</code>, or MERGE_AFTER_FIX with findings. A verdict covers one commit; any new commit needs a new verdict.</li>\n"
text pz19 "<li><strong>Fresh-clone gate with a negative control.</strong> The desk refuses unless the patch head equals the reviewed commit, <code>[ &quot;$H&quot; = &quot;&lt;reviewed commit&gt;&quot; ] || exit 1</code>, then clones fresh from the Radicle mirror and runs the repository's gate. A negative control, a known-bad input, must fail the same gate, or the gate proves nothing.</li>\n"
text pz20 "<li><strong>Merge.</strong> Only then is the patch merged into main, pushed to Radicle under the delegate key and announced to the seeds. NOT_RUN is never counted as PASS.</li>\n</ol>\n"
text pz21 "<h2>Worked examples from 7 Nov 2026</h2>\n<ul class='report-list'>\n"
text pzd1 "<li><strong>aien-sovereign-core-mv (core#925)</strong>: patch <a href='https://radicle.network/nodes/rosa.radicle.network/rad:z44GqrPVAPjZkhoD2MWVjqy18ighN/patches/f75aeaa5e019f2f58de614f17682badddf9aca5d'><code>f75aeaa5</code></a>, verdict MERGE at head <a href='https://radicle.network/nodes/rosa.radicle.network/rad:z44GqrPVAPjZkhoD2MWVjqy18ighN/commits/78f40e033bbcbb01549f1248b1d714cafcd4400d'><code>78f40e03</code></a>, revised once on review, merged as a fast-forward to the reviewed head. Gate: fresh clone of the Radicle mirror: build, 88/88 cases, 31 table checks PASS; negative control (the old cockpit main) fails 44 HTTP checks, as it must.</li>\n"
text pzd2 "<li><strong>CUDApp#373</strong>: patch <a href='https://radicle.network/nodes/rosa.radicle.network/rad:z4RxD8vXigmWg61nM8miQ8DVPAXEP/patches/958571b55fb200d46e2f0a8cec367656c21c1f0a'><code>958571b5</code></a>, verdict MERGE at head <a href='https://radicle.network/nodes/rosa.radicle.network/rad:z4RxD8vXigmWg61nM8miQ8DVPAXEP/commits/9714eba8f1ff5bca218edb075386f813eb524d9d'><code>9714eba8</code></a>, an earlier head got MERGE_AFTER_FIX; the fixed head was re-reviewed and merged. Gate: fresh clone: encoder unit, golden and mutant suites pass; negative control (the base encoder) fails the new gate.</li>\n"
text pzd3 "<li><strong>omega-bridge#79</strong>: patch <a href='https://radicle.network/nodes/rosa.radicle.network/rad:z3Hr9ZaiKHwwuNzPK5M8c7uw6pj7y/patches/3a95f707b281d49739d63dbd4581163f44d427a1'><code>3a95f707</code></a>, verdict MERGE at head <a href='https://radicle.network/nodes/rosa.radicle.network/rad:z3Hr9ZaiKHwwuNzPK5M8c7uw6pj7y/commits/882e3c061723205fbaf34c8a949e1be3451ac9e7'><code>882e3c06</code></a>, merged as a fast-forward to the reviewed head. Gate: fresh clone: receipt checker golden and mutant tests and all suites pass; negative control (a wrong compiler) is refused.</li>\n"
text pzd4 "<li><strong>omega-mv (tape padding check)</strong>: patch <a href='https://radicle.network/nodes/rosa.radicle.network/rad:z6do9WDBhuSnvopDkgFdFr1yWA62/patches/4dd099df31792d5ddb0d9fac5ca6d568513f4539'><code>4dd099df</code></a>, verdict MERGE at head <a href='https://radicle.network/nodes/rosa.radicle.network/rad:z6do9WDBhuSnvopDkgFdFr1yWA62/commits/215ea39afdc0cf1914cfadf43bbb6d23ce68c920'><code>215ea39a</code></a>, merged as a fast-forward to the reviewed head. Gate: fresh clone: tape suite passes 351 checks; four mutants fail it, as they must; the base commit runs only 302 checks.</li>\n"
text pzd5 "<li><strong>omega-mv (bench baseline)</strong>: patch <a href='https://radicle.network/nodes/rosa.radicle.network/rad:z6do9WDBhuSnvopDkgFdFr1yWA62/patches/88050ef7d710cb43d65214ff50bb1a0882770bb9'><code>88050ef7</code></a>, verdict MERGE at head <a href='https://radicle.network/nodes/rosa.radicle.network/rad:z6do9WDBhuSnvopDkgFdFr1yWA62/commits/3743d642cf034299009936eb8d458ba96a0a8589'><code>3743d642</code></a>, merged with merge commit da8b7e66 onto 215ea39a after a separate approval. Gate: fresh clone at the merge commit: integrity check and bench gate pass; negative controls (a wrong expected value, a swapped manifest) fail, as they must.</li>\n"
text pzd6 "<li><strong>aien-architecture-mv#382</strong> (ADR 0046): <span class='pill wait'>HELD</span> The reviewer returned MERGE_AFTER_FIX at head <code>6daec174</code>, so it stays unmerged until a fixed head earns a MERGE verdict.</li>\n</ul>\n"
text pz22 "<h2>Try it</h2>\n<pre><code class='language-sh' aria-label='Clone from Radicle and replicate'># with the Radicle CLI (radicle.xyz)\nrad clone rad:zNhNbqYvgSBEHBq9vvE8xpbcBzGa    # interplane-mv\nrad clone rad:z6do9WDBhuSnvopDkgFdFr1yWA62    # omega-mv\nrad clone rad:z631r2JJiVT8it4tST7RK24hpowi    # cuda-crack\n# or with plain git, from the read-only mirror\ngit clone https://www.aienos.com/rad/zNhNbqYvgSBEHBq9vvE8xpbcBzGa.git\n# replicate the host work from Radicle in a clean userspace\ncurl -fsSL https://www.aienos.com/replicate | sh</code></pre>\n"
text pz23 "<h2>Roadmap</h2>\n<p>Everything in this section is planned, not running. It will be listed under What runs today only when it runs.</p>\n<ul class='stage-list'>\n"
text pz24 "<li><span class='pill none'>PLANNED</span> <strong>forge decide as the merge step</strong>: the merge rule above (exact-head verdict, fresh-clone gate, negative control) is written as a seeded Omega core, <code>forge/forge.om</code> in interplane-mv. It is HOST TESTED on the Spark: it replays real desk decisions (two MERGE, one HOLD) and its test suite catches every mutant. No forge runner applies it to patches yet, so merges still go through the desk protocol above. It reads Radicle through the <code>rad</code> and <code>git</code> command line tools; a native Omega reader is planned.</li>\n"
text pz25 "<li><span class='pill none'>PLANNED</span> <strong>Review in the web app</strong>: READY files, verdicts and gate results beside each patch.</li>\n"
text pz26 "<li><span class='pill none'>PLANNED</span> <strong>Issue workflow</strong>: issues tied to patches and verdicts, beyond today's read-only lists.</li>\n"
text pz27 "<li><span class='pill none'>PLANNED</span> <strong>CI runners</strong>: gate runners that report back to the desk.</li>\n"
text pz28 "<li><span class='pill none'>PLANNED</span> <strong>Review federation</strong>: accepting signed verdicts from reviewers on other nodes.</li>\n</ul>\n"
text pz29 "<h2>Built on Radicle</h2>\n<p>Forge is a workflow and a set of gates on top of <a href='https://radicle.xyz/'>Radicle</a>, the peer-to-peer code collaboration stack, and its protocol implementation <a href='https://radicle.network/nodes/rosa.radicle.network/rad:z3gqcJUoA1n9HaHKufZs5FCSGazv5'>Heartwood</a>. Radicle is built by the Radicle team, not by this project. Repositories, patches, signatures and seeding are Radicle's; the merge rule is INTERPLANE Forge's.</p>\n"

note routes (routes.rs): slug, label, description; the forge page header differs from its label
text pu1 "quick-start"
text pu2 "concepts"
text pu3 "adapter"
text pu4 "conformance"
text pu5 "status"
text pu6 "forge"
text pt1 "Quick Start"
text pt2 "Concepts"
text pt3 "Writing an Adapter"
text pt4 "Conformance"
text pt5 "Versioned Status"
text pt6 "Forge"
text pd1 "Run INTERPLANE's pinned scripted offline example and inspect denied actions and held approvals without a model or GPU."
text pd2 "Understand the model, protocol and runtime boundary: proposed intent is not authority, and the runtime retains execution and approval control."
text pd3 "Follow INTERPLANE's canonical pinned Rust adapter guide, host-owned decisions and conformance requirements without assuming universal support."
text pd4 "Trace INTERPLANE conformance, refusals and reported results to source-pinned fixtures and evidence, including failed and planned stages."
text pd5 "Read INTERPLANE's versioned source status and exact Spark verification verdict from the canonical generated facts."
text pd6 "INTERPLANE Forge, a GitHub replacement being built on Radicle: agents open patches, while exact-head verdicts, gates and people keep merge authority."
text ph6 "INTERPLANE Forge"
text pk1 "INTERPLANE / Developer documentation"
text pk6 "INTERPLANE / Forge"

note pp_purl: the Radicle web URL of the protocol repository
